ittle has out-raised Eric Pratt and holds an outside-spending edge", "Pratt's campaign hit by staffer resignation over white nationalist posts", "Raters lean Likely/Safe D and markets price Democrats near 92-93%"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a double-digit Democratic margin: a D+3 seat, a strong national environment, Little's fundraising and outside-spending advantage, and a September poll showing a 12-point lead. Pratt's staffer controversy adds to his headwinds, though the open seat and thin polling keep this short of Safe.", "watch": "A shift in the national environment toward Republicans or a late polling move by Pratt could narrow the race into tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Angie Craig (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Angie Craig's retirement leaves this D+3 Minneapolis-area seat open, with Democrat Matt Little facing Republican state Senator Eric Pratt. Little has raised roughly $923,000 to Pratt's $511,000 and benefits from outside spending on his side, while Pratt's campaign suffered a damaging story when a staffer resigned over white nationalist social media posts in September.\n\nA September live-caller poll showed Little ahead 52-40, and prediction markets price Democratic chances around 92-93%. Most expert raters call the race Likely D, with several rating it Safe. The combination of the district lean, the environment, and the money edge points to a Democratic hold, though the open seat and limited polling leave some room for a closer finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9565, "margin": 11.37}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9477, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9516, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9571, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9414, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9494, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9241, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9593, "margin":